# Anchored to the repository root, all three of them: `gallery/` unanchored also
# matched examples/gallery/, which kept that example's only source file out of
# the first commit and broke the build everywhere CI ran it.
# `/build*/` and not `/build/`: a second configuration is the normal way to
# check something — a Debug tree beside a Release one, a scratch tree to
# reproduce a CI failure — and every one of them was untracked only by luck.
# One of them reached a commit.
/build*/
/out/
/gallery/

# An **in-source** build, which the rules above do not catch because it has no
# directory of its own — it puts CMakeCache.txt, CMakeFiles/, a Makefile and
# every object file beside the sources. One stray `cmake .` in the repository
# root did exactly that, and the next `git add -A` committed 326 generated
# files. Anchored, because `tests/CMakeLists.txt` and friends are real.
/CMakeCache.txt
/CMakeFiles/
/Makefile
/cmake_install.cmake
/CTestTestfile.cmake
/gbuiConfig.cmake
/gbuiConfigVersion.cmake
/libgbui*.a
/libgbui*.so*
# And the same wreckage one directory down, which an in-source build also
# leaves in src/, tests/ and demos/.
demos/Makefile
tests/Makefile
tools/Makefile
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
*.o
*.o.d
node_modules/
docs/.vitepress/dist/
docs/.vitepress/cache/

# The WebAssembly demo bundle, and the Emscripten build that produces it.
# Built by tools/build_wasm.sh, and by CI before the site is published.
/build-wasm/
/build-wasm-debug/
docs/public/demo/

# Screenshots the examples write.
*.ppm

# Editor and tooling leftovers.
compile_commands.json
.cache/
.DS_Store

# The roadmap is a working document, not part of the published site.
ROADMAP.md
docs/roadmap.md
__pycache__/
